= Conclusion
<conclusion>

We have presented an end-to-end deep learning pipeline for chest X-ray analysis that combines classification, object detection, and semantic segmentation. The classification model achieves strong screening performance (ROC-AUC 0.93) and is suitable for use as a first-pass triage tool. The detection model localizes pneumonia opacities and could be used to highlight suspicious regions for radiologist review. The segmentation model produces pixel-level masks that are clinically interpretable and can be used for quantitative analysis of lesion size and progression.

The main limitation of this work is the small annotated dataset (50 images), which constrains the absolute performance of the detection and segmentation models. Future work will scale up the annotated dataset, explore semi-supervised learning to leverage the large unannotated training set, and integrate the three models into a single deployable web application with a clinician-facing dashboard.

